      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OKLAHOMA BALE (3) had a tricky draw and ran well to finish third, beaten 1.3 lengths, (25.56) at Ballarat. Makes plenty of appeal. PYRENEES ACE (6) wasn't far away at the finish when 5th and beaten only 4.5 lengths (23.81) at this track. Has a good record here at this journey. Goes well out of this box with a win and two minor placings. In the mix. RUXTON GIRL (1) produced a moderate effort last time when sixth at Bendigo over 425m behind Nosey Parker (24.74) in a Grade 5. Placed at her previous run. Form from her last run is proving to be solid. Should be thereabouts. Something for the Multiples: POWER EDITION (2)",
